{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837948",
      "title": "What Are Forms & What's Tricky About Them?",
      "sourceHash": "86ca85b719aca61f02be7a22bc2d5af12c302dbe73a406f63e3a2acd5aa87194",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "So what's so difficult about forms?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 8.97,
          "en": "Why do we need this special course section?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.97,
          "end": 13.97,
          "en": "Well, let's first of all define what exactly a form is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.58,
          "end": 18.84,
          "en": "And it is basically a collection of input fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.84,
          "end": 22.5,
          "en": "like this login form here, but also potentially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 27.45,
          "en": "like this more complex signup form we'll also explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 27.45,
          "end": 29.79,
          "en": "in this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.79,
          "end": 32.76,
          "en": "And technically, if you take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.76,
          "end": 35.01,
          "en": "at the code I am providing to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.01,
          "end": 37.65,
          "en": "as part of this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.65,
          "end": 41.85,
          "en": "a form is simply a collection of input fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.85,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "which typically are used in conjunction with labels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 50.04,
          "en": "that are wrapped by the form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 53.823,
          "en": "the built-in HTML form element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "That's what a form is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 60.39,
          "en": "But what's now so difficult about forms?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.39,
          "end": 64.53,
          "en": "Well, in the end, forms are about two main things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.53,
          "end": 66.54,
          "en": "you wanna do with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "You wanna handle their submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 72.96000000000001,
          "en": "and extract the values entered by the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.96000000000001,
          "end": 77.85,
          "en": "and you typically also want to validate the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.85,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "that's provided by the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 83.19,
          "en": "and show some validation errors to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.19,
          "end": 86.283,
          "en": "if incorrect data has been provided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 91.5,
          "en": "Now, thankfully, handling the form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.5,
          "end": 96.5,
          "en": "is relatively easy and so is the extraction of entered data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 97.74000000000001,
          "end": 102.12,
          "en": "You can, for example, manage that data via state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 106.92,
          "en": "as you already learned it, by setting up two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 106.92,
          "end": 109.28999999999999,
          "en": "And we'll revisit this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 109.28999999999999,
          "end": 111.333,
          "en": "in this section here, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 112.44,
          "end": 116.00999999999999,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could consider using refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.00999999999999,
          "end": 117.66,
          "en": "to extract values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.66,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "And we'll, of course. also revisit this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 126.3,
          "en": "Or, and that will be new in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 126.3,
          "end": 130.95,
          "en": "you could use built-in features provided by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 130.95,
          "end": 135.15,
          "en": "to extract and get that data entered by the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 135.15,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "into those form fields with help of the form data object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 141.45,
          "en": "And you will learn how to use that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 141.45,
          "end": 143.163,
          "en": "in this section, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144.18,
          "end": 146.444,
          "en": "But as you will see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 146.444,
          "end": 149.73,
          "en": "this part is typically not the difficult part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 154.73,
          "en": "Extracting data is typically quite straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "Instead, it's that validation part that can be tricky,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 164.34,
          "en": "especially if you wanna provide a good user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 167.37,
          "en": "Because as you will see in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 167.37,
          "end": 171.09,
          "en": "you could validate the data entered by the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 171.09,
          "end": 174.09,
          "en": "on every keystroke and show an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 174.09,
          "end": 177.57,
          "en": "if the user enters something invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 177.57,
          "end": 179.37,
          "en": "But if you are doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.37,
          "end": 183.393,
          "en": "errors may be shown too early, as you will see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 184.62,
          "end": 187.11,
          "en": "Therefore, alternatively,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 187.11,
          "end": 191.1,
          "en": "you could validate whenever the user is done typing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 191.1,
          "end": 194.97,
          "en": "into an input field and that field loses focus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 194.97,
          "end": 197.73,
          "en": "But in that case, as you will see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 197.73,
          "end": 199.95,
          "en": "one potential problem can be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 199.95,
          "end": 203.313,
          "en": "that errors may be showing up for too long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 204.78,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "You could also simply validate upon form submission,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 212.1,
          "en": "but depending on your app's requirements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 212.1,
          "end": 214.89,
          "en": "and the user experience you wanna offer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 214.89,
          "end": 219.66,
          "en": "in that case, you may be showing error messages too late.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 219.66,
          "end": 223.26,
          "en": "And therefore we'll explore these different approaches,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 223.26,
          "end": 226.41,
          "en": "and we'll also explore how we can combine them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 226.41,
          "end": 230.07,
          "en": "so that you can then thereafter at the end of this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 230.07,
          "end": 234.24,
          "en": "make the best choice for your app and your users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 234.24,
          "end": 237.753,
          "en": "and also implement that solution you wanna go for.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}